  "id": "BIT-tomcat-2026-118028",
  "summary": "Apache Tomcat: RewriteValve [F]/[G]/[R] rule matches do not stop processing",
  "details": "Execution After Redirect (EAR) vulnerability in Apache Tomcat in RedirectValve affecting flags [F], [G] and [R].\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Tomcat: from 11.0.0 through 11.0.27, from 10.1.20 through 10.1.61, from 9.0.87 through 9.0.123.\n\n\n\nThe following versions were EOL at the time the CVE was created but are known to be affected: 8.5.100. Other unsupported versions may also be affected.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 11.0.29, 10.1.62, 9.0.124, which fixes the issue.\nNote: Tomcat 11.0.28 was not released",
